      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield%2C_Vermont",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Black River’s 110‑foot drop over a short stretch powered early cotton mills, card factories, and even bucket factories in Springfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield%2C_Vermont",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Springfield’s Machine Tool Trail lets drivers walk through the town’s industrial past, highlighting its shift to a precision‑tool center in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.vermonter.com/explore-springfield-vermont/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Hartness State Airport, named after James Hartness, sits on land he donated in 1931 and reflects Springfield’s aviation heritage.",
